<article class="env-definition" id="01U3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01U3">Definition <span data-tag="01U3">29.26.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>flat at a point $x \in X$</em> if the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ is flat over the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{S, f(x)}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say that $\mathcal{F}$ is <em>flat over $S$ at a point $x \in X$</em> if the stalk $\mathcal{F}_ x$ is a flat $\mathcal{O}_{S, f(x)}$-module. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>flat</em> if $f$ is flat at every point of $X$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say that $\mathcal{F}$ is <em>flat over $S$</em> if $\mathcal{F}$ is flat over $S$ at every point $x$ of $X$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>